# SFT execution status v0.129: concrete output-parent mismatch reproduced and fixed locally

2026-09-28. **280 local tests passed; zero failures, errors or skips. Ruff
passed.** A deterministic native-layout incompatibility is reproduced in the
frozen coordinator's actual validator and coordinator control flow. The v3
entry corrects the layout without relaxing the path gate. No AWS action,
native retry, GPU, real checkpoint access, inference or training occurred.

## Concrete defect

The v1/v2 entry selects `/work/import-attempt`. Inside the coordinator,
`parent = attempt.parent` is `/work`, followed by `_path(parent)`. The frozen
validator requires at least three Path.parts; `/work` has only two. It thus
raises `path_rejected` before creating the attempt directory. Prior local
integration substituted a longer temporary path, inadvertently hiding the
native-depth mismatch.

A regression calls the unchanged validator on exactly `/work` and proves
rejection before filesystem inspection. Another calls the actual coordinator
with generated controls and the old native output path, substituting only
host runtime/other namespace observations, and observes `path_rejected`
before mkdir. This establishes a real defect in the dispatched layout; the
previous native exit 47 did not preserve the internal rejection code, so it
does not retrospectively prove that this was its first failing check or its
only issue. No such stronger claim is made.

## Narrow correction

The new fixed v3 entry uses `/work/imports/attempt`. After all controls are
validated and the entry is marked consumed, it exclusively creates the parent
`/work/imports` with mode 0700. Existing parents are rejected, not reused.
The pre-creation writable-filesystem probe uses the existing `/work` root,
not the not-yet-created parent. The coordinator still creates the actual
attempt and applies its original depth, ownership, permissions, symlink and
overlap checks. All original admission, resource and accounting gates remain.
The extra parent directory is within the existing bounded tmpfs; no cumulative
native write quota is claimed.

V3 supervisor/launcher/source-builder differ from v2 only in versioned file,
release-root and unit-name bindings, checked by exact textual normalization.
Parser/control helper function ASTs match v2. The generated fixture and frozen
coordinator/kernel/loader/package sources were not changed. Diagnostic fixed
exit-code transport remains in place. Source bundle v0.4 and staging v3 are
prepared but were not uploaded or run.

## Evidence and limitations

- 16 new regression tests plus 264 prior tests passed in 5.928 seconds.
- Actual tiny generated conversion, two input audits, packaging and independent
  checksum verification passed with local host observations substituted.
- New regressions cover exact old path rejection, coordinator rejection before
  writes, correct new private parent, rejection of reused parents/no retry,
  invalid controls creating no parent and correct pre-creation filesystem probe.
- Parent audit hook recorded zero network/real-artifact violations. It is not
  OS isolation and is not claimed to propagate into child interpreters.
- Ruff passed for all six new Python files. All 49 source hashes in the new
  51-member archive match the workspace; all ten previous prepared bindings
  remain unchanged. Previous failed attempts are preserved.

